    <h2 class="section-title">About Me</h2>
    <p>
      Passionate about executing IT projects, my journey in software engineering is a dynamic quest to solve intricate
      puzzles and create real-world solutions. From manipulating gameplay through server programming to developing
      advanced localized neural network software, I thrive on the challenges of the ever-evolving IT landscape.
    </p>
    <p>
      Beginning with groundbreaking projects at the Brookhaven Synchrotron Laboratory, I contributed to publications in
      the New England Journal of Medicine, pioneering advancements in biophysics. Transitioning to pharmaceuticals and
      engineering, I became adept at troubleshooting real-world applications, providing critical data during drilling
      operations at Halliburton.
    </p>
    <p>
      Entrepreneurial at heart, I founded Propurty, a SaaS company, managing diverse projects across the property
      management and maintenance industry. Proficient in a variety of technology stacks, I initiate RFP, RFI, and SOW,
      crafting EULA agreements and merger agreements to accelerate company growth against competition.
    </p>
    <p>
      Beyond work, I stay abreast of technology trends, currently developing advanced localized neural network software.
      My leadership aims to facilitate operations, maximize revenue, and ensure strategic growth for businesses aligning
      with my interests — bridging the gap between cutting-edge technology and impactful solutions.
    </p>
